%% Before/After Fix Diagram
%% Shows the decorator syntax error fix for infra/celery/dags/celery.py

graph LR
    classDef badBox fill:#ffebee,stroke:#f44336,stroke-width:2px
    classDef goodBox fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50,stroke-width:2px
    classDef noteBox fill:#f5f5f5,stroke:#9e9e9e,stroke-dasharray:5 5

    subgraph Before["Before (INCORRECT)"]
        B1["@dag(...)"]
        B2["def celery():@task(executor='celery')<br/>Parse Error"]
        B3["Expected class, function definition, or async function definition after decorator"]
        B1 -->|invalid syntax| B2
        B2 --- B3
    end

    subgraph After["After (CORRECT)"]
        A1["@dag(...)"]
        A2["def celery():"]
        A3["    @task(queue='cpu')"]
        A4["    def a():"]
        A5["        print('A')"]
        A6["        sleep(15)"]
        A1 -->|valid| A2
        A2 -->|indented| A3
        A3 -->|indented| A4
        A4 -->|indented| A5
        A5 -->|indented| A6
    end

    B2 -.->|fix applied| A2

    takeaway["Key Takeaways:<br/>1. Always put decorators on their own line<br/>2. Indent @task functions inside the @dag function<br/>3. Use @task(queue='...') for Celery queue routing"]:::noteBox
    B2 -.-> takeaway

    class Before badBox
    class After goodBox
